# --- Database field encryption (REQUIRED) -----------------------------------
# 64 hex chars (32 bytes). Every field in MongoDB is AES-256-GCM encrypted with keys derived
# from this. BACK IT UP SEPARATELY from the database: if it is lost, the data is unrecoverable.
# Do not change it once data exists (rotation needs a re-encrypt migration).
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
